00:52:28.060 --> 00:52:33.820
it cuts to a shot of the puppet, and the puppet can't speak, and we lost it.
镜头切到了木偶，木偶不会说话，我们当时都笑场了。

1544
00:52:33.900 --> 00:52:36.400
The puppet is like a gape, right?
木偶当时是张着嘴的，对吧？

1545
00:52:36.520 --> 00:52:37.880
His mouth is open.
他的嘴是张开的。

1546
00:52:38.380 --> 00:52:43.080
Do you know that the puppet, they linger on the puppet with its mouth open in silence,
你知道吗，那个木偶，他们让镜头在木偶张着嘴沉默的画面上停留了很久，

1547
00:52:43.080 --> 00:52:45.080
like, what the heck, right?
就像在说，搞什么鬼，对吧？

1548
00:52:45.240 --> 00:52:45.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1549
00:52:45.420 --> 00:52:49.060
They linger on that puppet for six seconds of silence.
他们在那个木偶身上停留了六秒钟的沉默。

1550
00:52:49.300 --> 00:52:49.480
Oh.
哦。

1551
00:52:49.960 --> 00:52:57.340
I mean, seeing a puppet with its mouth agape, being like, what the eff is going on?
我是说，看到一个木偶张着大嘴，心想这到底是什么鬼？

1552
00:52:58.080 --> 00:52:59.740
It is funny.
挺好笑的。

1553
00:52:59.980 --> 00:53:00.440
It is.
确实。

1554
00:53:00.520 --> 00:53:01.280
It is funny.
真的挺好笑的。

1555
00:53:01.580 --> 00:53:03.500
And when we were shooting this-
当时我们在拍这一段的时候——

1556
00:53:03.500 --> 00:53:04.340
Six seconds.
六秒钟。

1557
00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:06.560
We were dying.
我们都快笑死了。

1558
00:53:06.900 --> 00:53:07.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1559
00:53:07.160 --> 00:53:09.660
We were dying at the shot of the puppet.
我们看到木偶那个镜头时都快笑疯了。

1560
00:53:10.280 --> 00:53:14.880
And so when I was getting ready, I think, to sit down and watch this scene, all I could
所以当我准备坐下来看这一幕的时候，我满脑子

1561
00:53:14.880 --> 00:53:19.060
remember was how we were crying laughing at this reaction shot of the puppet.
想到的都是我们当时看着木偶那个反应镜头笑得流眼泪的样子。

1562
00:53:20.500 --> 00:53:27.780
But then I saw, I just saw this whole other side of how not funny that was.
但后来我看到了，我看到了它完全不搞笑的另一面。

1563
00:53:27.860 --> 00:53:44.840
Well, we were looking at the puppet.
嗯，我们当时盯着木偶看呢。

1564
00:53:44.840 --> 00:53:47.920
The kids start peppering Michael with questions, right?
孩子们开始连珠炮似地问迈克尔问题，对吧？

1565
00:53:48.200 --> 00:53:48.440
Yeah.
对。

1566
00:53:48.560 --> 00:53:49.900
They're saying, well, did you get married?
他们问，你结婚了吗？

1567
00:53:49.980 --> 00:53:50.660
Do you have kids?
你有孩子吗？

1568
00:53:50.780 --> 00:53:51.400
Do you have a girlfriend?
你有女朋友吗？

1569
00:53:51.940 --> 00:53:56.160
And then the little girl says, I guess you didn't get to be what you wanted to be.
然后那个小女孩说，我猜你没能成为你想成为的人。

1570
00:53:56.960 --> 00:53:57.400
Ugh.
呃。

1571
00:53:57.400 --> 00:54:00.400
And it is soul crushing.
那真是太扎心了。

1572
00:54:00.700 --> 00:54:03.040
And I was watching this with Isabel, who's 11.
我当时和11岁的伊莎贝尔一起看。

1573
00:54:03.640 --> 00:54:09.300
And she turned to me and she goes, Mom, were there just times when you were doing this show
她转过头对我说，妈妈，你在拍这部剧的时候，

1574
00:54:09.300 --> 00:54:11.920
that you were like, I am so uncomfortable?
有没有觉得特别尴尬的时候？

1575
00:54:12.600 --> 00:54:12.940
Mm.
嗯。

1576
00:54:13.560 --> 00:54:15.480
She was like, this is really uncomfortable.
她说，这真的让人很不舒服。

1577
00:54:16.340 --> 00:54:19.340
I mean, she thought it was funny, you know, but she was like, that is awkward.
我是说，她觉得这很有趣，你知道的，但她觉得那真的很尴尬。

1578
00:54:19.340 --> 00:54:20.400
And I was like, yeah.
我就说，是啊。

1579
00:54:20.640 --> 00:54:21.160
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

1580
00:54:21.160 --> 00:54:25.920
There are a lot of cringey moments on this show, which make it all work in balance.
这部剧里有很多让人尴尬的时刻，这让整部剧保持了一种平衡。

1581
00:54:25.980 --> 00:54:31.260
But just the fact that she picked up on that at her age of like, what an awkward moment this was.
但她小小年纪就能察觉到那一刻有多尴尬，这真的很让人感慨。

1582
00:54:31.820 --> 00:54:32.560
Oh, man.
天哪。

1583
00:54:33.140 --> 00:54:35.200
Well, Michael is so gutted, he juSt.
迈克尔太难过了，他直接……

1584
00:54:35.420 --> 00:54:36.880
He locks himself in his office.
他把自己锁在办公室里。

1585
00:54:37.040 --> 00:54:37.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1586
00:54:37.460 --> 00:54:38.160
He won't come out.
他不肯出来。

1587
00:54:38.680 --> 00:54:41.980
And the reaction shots of all of us are great.
我们所有人的反应镜头都很棒。

1588
00:54:41.980 --> 00:54:44.320
We're all really sad for him.
我们都真心为他感到难过。

1589
00:54:46.060 --> 00:54:47.680
Sad, a little embarrassed.
难过，还有点尴尬。

1590
00:54:47.760 --> 00:54:48.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1591
00:54:48.400 --> 00:54:48.960
All of it.
各种情绪都有。

1592
00:54:51.380 --> 00:54:53.100
So, Pam's talking to Jim.
所以，帕姆在和吉姆说话。

1593
00:54:53.220 --> 00:54:55.460
We got a lot of mail about this little scene.
我们收到了很多关于这一小段戏的邮件。

1594
00:54:56.580 --> 00:54:58.080
Pam's talking to Jim.
帕姆在和吉姆说话。

1595
00:54:58.240 --> 00:55:00.160
She's saying Michael won't come out of his office.
她说迈克尔不肯出办公室。

1596
00:55:00.160 --> 00:55:01.380
He won't answer his phone.
他不接电话。

1597
00:55:01.820 --> 00:55:05.660
Over her shoulder, Roy is wrestling with Meredith's son.
在她身后，罗伊正在和梅雷迪思的儿子打闹。

1598
00:55:05.780 --> 00:55:06.660
He's so happy.
他玩得好开心。

1599
00:55:06.960 --> 00:55:07.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1600
00:55:07.240 --> 00:55:10.060
Roy and the jerk kid are having the best time.
罗伊和那个讨厌的小孩玩得可开心了。

1601
00:55:10.180 --> 00:55:13.200
We had a lot of questions about what this scene was supposed to mean.
我们收到了很多关于这一幕到底是什么意思的提问。

1602
00:55:13.200 --> 00:55:19.080
Because Pam seems a little bit embarrassed or ashamed that Roy and this kid are getting along.
因为帕姆看起来有点尴尬，或者说为罗伊和这个孩子相处得这么好感到羞愧。

1603
00:55:19.200 --> 00:55:20.200
They're like, what did this mean?
他们都在问，这到底是什么意思？

1604
00:55:21.540 --> 00:55:25.180
Well, I think, I don't know.
嗯，我想，我也不知道。

1605
00:55:25.300 --> 00:55:26.640
What was your interpretation here?
你对这一幕是怎么解读的？

1606
00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:27.540
Here was my take on it.
我是这么看的。

1607
00:55:27.600 --> 00:55:27.800
Okay.
好的。

1608
00:55:27.800 --> 00:55:31.100
Because you have Roy, this big guy, right?
因为罗伊是个大块头，对吧？

1609
00:55:31.280 --> 00:55:32.620
And he's kind of fratty.
他有点像那种兄弟会的人。

1610
00:55:32.740 --> 00:55:33.980
He's kind of like a frat guy.
他就像个兄弟会男生。

1611
00:55:34.460 --> 00:55:37.340
And he is with the kid that's the asshole.
而他正和那个混蛋小孩待在一起。

1612
00:55:37.580 --> 00:55:37.900
Right.
没错。

1613
00:55:38.000 --> 00:55:39.840
And they're having the time of their lives.
他们玩得正开心呢。

1614
00:55:39.980 --> 00:55:40.740
They're in there.
他们就在那儿。

1615
00:55:40.940 --> 00:55:42.760
There's other people around them.
周围还有其他人。

1616
00:55:42.860 --> 00:55:45.720
They're not even caring about other people's personal space.
他们根本不在乎别人的私人空间。

1617
00:55:45.860 --> 00:55:47.700
They're wrestling in this room.
他们在房间里摔跤。

1618
00:55:47.820 --> 00:55:49.460
And Roy's like, got him in a headlock.
罗伊还把他锁喉了。

1619
00:55:49.540 --> 00:55:50.860
And he's like, I love this kid.
他就像是说，我喜欢这孩子。

1620
00:55:50.860 --> 00:55:57.560
And I think Pam had a flash of what her life would be like with Roy, with children.
我觉得帕姆那一瞬间预见到了她和罗伊有了孩子后的生活会是什么样。

1621
00:55:57.840 --> 00:55:59.420
What their kids would be like.
他们的孩子会是什么样。

1622
00:55:59.600 --> 00:55:59.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1623
00:56:00.240 --> 00:56:02.880
She's going to have a kid that's like, mom, pull my finger.
她以后会有一个孩子，会说：妈，快拉我的手指。

1624
00:56:03.160 --> 00:56:03.440
Fart.
放个屁。

1625
00:56:03.660 --> 00:56:04.320
Dad, laugh.
爸，快笑啊。

1626
00:56:04.860 --> 00:56:05.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1627
00:56:05.620 --> 00:56:06.840
And Pam was like, oh, God.
帕姆当时心想，天哪。

1628
00:56:07.100 --> 00:56:07.540
Well.
嗯。

1629
00:56:07.540 --> 00:56:07.940
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1630
00:56:08.060 --> 00:56:12.320
I'm going to be outnumbered in my own house by like the Roy kids.
我在自己家里要被这群罗伊式的小孩给淹没了。

1631
00:56:12.740 --> 00:56:13.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1632
00:56:13.240 --> 00:56:19.040
I think it's definitely there to show a contrast to the way Jim bonds with a kid.
我觉得这绝对是为了对比吉姆和孩子相处的方式。

1633
00:56:19.300 --> 00:56:19.480
Yeah.
没错。

1634
00:56:19.480 --> 00:56:21.040
Over books and reading.
通过书本和阅读。

1635
00:56:21.600 --> 00:56:22.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1636
00:56:22.160 --> 00:56:23.840
As opposed to just roughhousing.
而不是单纯的打闹。

1637
00:56:24.500 --> 00:56:24.700
Yeah.
没错。

1638
00:56:24.820 --> 00:56:31.180
But I have to say, when I saw that, I thought, yes, that's what this kid needs, actually.
但我不得不说，当我看到那一幕时，我想，是的，这其实正是这孩子所需要的。

1639
00:56:31.340 --> 00:56:34.340
He needs a father figure in his life.
他生命中需要一个父亲形象。

1640
00:56:34.540 --> 00:56:34.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1641
00:56:34.640 --> 00:56:36.160
He needs someone to wrestle with him.
他需要有人陪他摔跤。

1642
00:56:36.260 --> 00:56:38.500
Because that is an important part of parenting.
因为那是育儿中很重要的一部分。

1643
00:56:38.640 --> 00:56:42.820
I didn't think that that was so bad of a thing.
我觉得这并不是什么坏事。

1644
00:56:42.960 --> 00:56:43.180
No.
没错。

1645
00:56:43.180 --> 00:56:44.800
I think it's perfect for Roy.
我觉得这很适合罗伊。

1646
00:56:44.960 --> 00:56:48.400
The problem is that's not what Pam wants in a dad.
问题在于，这并不是帕姆想要的父亲形象。

1647
00:56:48.400 --> 00:56:54.440
Pam wants more of a Jim dad that is going to do a silly dance and talk about books and
帕姆想要的是像吉姆那样的爸爸，会跳滑稽的舞，谈论书籍，

1648
00:56:54.440 --> 00:56:55.860
probably wrestle a little bit, too.
可能也会稍微摔跤一下。

1649
00:56:56.260 --> 00:56:58.400
But I think Roy is just a little brutish.
但我认为罗伊确实有点粗鲁。

1650
00:56:58.520 --> 00:57:00.580
It's absolutely what Meredith's son needs.
这绝对是梅雷迪思的儿子所需要的。

1651
00:57:00.800 --> 00:57:03.740
I mean, he needs a big guy to grab him and be like, hey.
我的意思是，他需要一个大块头去抓住他，然后说，嘿。

1652
00:57:04.060 --> 00:57:04.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1653
00:57:04.480 --> 00:57:05.400
You know, pay attention.
你知道，注意点。

1654
00:57:05.800 --> 00:57:11.900
But I just think it's just that moment that shows that Jim and Pam are just, you know,
但我只是觉得那一刻展现了吉姆和帕姆，你知道，

1655
00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:12.720
you meet people.
你会遇到各种人。

1656
00:57:12.880 --> 00:57:14.240
We all like dated people.
我们都和不同的人约会过。

1657
00:57:14.420 --> 00:57:18.300
And there's some people you know instinctively that you're going to parent the same with.
有些人你凭直觉就知道，你们的育儿方式会是一样的。

1658
00:57:18.400 --> 00:57:18.640
Yeah.
没错。

1659
00:57:18.640 --> 00:57:20.980
And I think Pam and Jim are going to parent the same.
我觉得帕姆和吉姆的育儿方式会是一样的。

1660
00:57:21.240 --> 00:57:21.500
Yes.
是的。

1661
00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:22.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1662
00:57:22.540 --> 00:57:23.480
I think that's good.
我觉得这很好。

1663
00:57:23.780 --> 00:57:24.380
That's good.
那很好。

1664
00:57:24.440 --> 00:57:25.120
That's good analysis.
分析得很好。

1665
00:57:25.460 --> 00:57:26.080
I like that.
我喜欢这个观点。

1666
00:57:26.680 --> 00:57:30.040
Well, next up, we go to the copier with Dwight.
好了，接下来，我们要去复印机那里看看德怀特。

1667
00:57:30.100 --> 00:57:32.980
And we're going to see how Dwight might parent Jake.
我们要看看德怀特会怎么教育杰克。

1668
00:57:33.640 --> 00:57:35.800
Well, again, Dwight and Angela.
嗯，再说一次，德怀特和安吉拉。

1669
00:57:36.040 --> 00:57:39.140
Angela has told him he needs to be tougher with the kids.
安吉拉告诉过他，他对孩子们需要更严厉一点。

1670
00:57:39.280 --> 00:57:42.260
Basically, that's her subtext because that's what she would expect.
基本上，这就是她的潜台词，因为那是她所期望的。

1671
00:57:42.500 --> 00:57:42.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1672
00:57:42.780 --> 00:57:42.920
Right?
对吧？

1673
00:57:43.120 --> 00:57:44.520
That's what she had growing up.
她从小就是那样长大的。

1674
00:57:44.600 --> 00:57:46.120
And she expects him to be that way.
所以她也期望他那样做。

1675
00:57:46.500 --> 00:57:46.880
Yeah.
没错。

1676
00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:48.880
So she's egging him on.
所以她在怂恿他。

1677
00:57:49.100 --> 00:57:49.620
She is.
确实是。

1678
00:57:49.900 --> 00:57:52.660
She's like glaring at him like, shut the kid up.
她瞪着他，好像在说，让那孩子闭嘴。

1679
00:57:52.840 --> 00:57:55.180
Jake tells Dwight that he's ugly.
杰克告诉德怀特他很丑。

1680
00:57:55.700 --> 00:57:56.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1681
00:57:56.460 --> 00:57:59.620
And then Dwight is horrible.
然后德怀特表现得太糟糕了。

1682
00:57:59.820 --> 00:58:00.300
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

1683
00:58:00.580 --> 00:58:00.760
At my prodding.
是在我的怂恿下。

1684
00:58:00.840 --> 00:58:02.160
At my prodding, he's horrible.
是在我的怂恿下，他才表现得那么糟糕。

1685
00:58:02.420 --> 00:58:03.800
Can I get my mini soapbox out again?
我能再发表一下我的个人观点吗？

1686
00:58:04.060 --> 00:58:05.600
Because I did not care for this.
因为我不太喜欢这一段。

1687
00:58:05.760 --> 00:58:06.580
No, it wasn't good.
不，这表现得不好。

1688
00:58:06.900 --> 00:58:08.000
It bumped me.
这让我感到不适。

1689
00:58:08.920 --> 00:58:15.060
I didn't like that Dwight told a child, like that Dwight insulted a child the way he did.
我不喜欢德怀特对一个孩子那样，不喜欢他那样侮辱一个孩子。

1690
00:58:15.220 --> 00:58:15.940
I didn't.
我真的不喜欢。

1691
00:58:15.940 --> 00:58:20.640
I think we're meant as an audience to be like, yeah, you give it to the jerk kid.
我觉得作为观众，我们本该觉得，没错，就该教训一下这个混蛋小孩。

1692
00:58:20.820 --> 00:58:22.260
But I just that.
但我只是……

1693
00:58:22.620 --> 00:58:24.060
Oh, I didn't like it.
噢，我不喜欢那样。

1694
00:58:24.180 --> 00:58:25.400
I don't think we're meant to do that.
我不觉得我们本该那样想。

1695
00:58:25.540 --> 00:58:26.020
You don't think?
你不觉得吗？

1696
00:58:26.180 --> 00:58:26.640
I don't think so.
我不这么认为。

1697
00:58:26.680 --> 00:58:32.320
I think like there's part of you that's like glad that this kid is like at least put in
我觉得你内心深处会有一部分觉得，很高兴这个孩子至少被

1698
00:58:32.320 --> 00:58:35.760
his place a little bit, although done completely inappropriately.
稍微教训了一下，尽管方式完全不妥当。

1699
00:58:36.420 --> 00:58:41.980
But I think what I took away from it is like, Dwight, Dwight is a kid.
但我从中领悟到的是，德怀特，德怀特自己就是个孩子。

1700
00:58:42.420 --> 00:58:43.100
You have two.
你有两个孩子。

1701
00:58:43.380 --> 00:58:45.320
These are two kids in one conversation.
这是两个孩子在一段对话中。

1702
00:58:45.880 --> 00:58:48.660
I mean, Isabel watched it with me and she was like, oh, mom, Dwight.
我是说，伊莎贝尔和我一起看的时候，她说，哦，妈妈，是德怀特。

1703
00:58:48.840 --> 00:58:50.160
And I said, I know he's just a kid.
我说，我知道，他只是个孩子。

1704
00:58:50.660 --> 00:58:53.500
Well, it all just made me super sad for Jake.
嗯，这一切让我为杰克感到非常难过。

1705
00:58:53.500 --> 00:58:56.100
Oh, well, Jake, Jake is doomed.
哦，好吧，杰克，杰克注定要倒霉了。

1706
00:58:56.720 --> 00:58:58.000
That's what I felt like.
我当时就是这种感觉。

